            0.063
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Number Play"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.087,
            0.848,
            0.164
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Aryabhata II’s (c. 950 CE) work Mahāsiddhānta, mentions the method of computing the digital root of a number by repeatedly adding the digits till a single-digit number is obtained. This method is known to have been used to perform checks on calculations of arithmetic operations."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.172,
            0.293,
            0.193
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Figure it Out"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.196,
            0.847,
            0.235
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. The digital root of an 8-digit number is 5. What will be the digital root of 10 more than that number?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.245,
            0.849,
            0.302
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. Write any number. Generate a sequence of numbers by repeatedly adding 11. What would be the digital roots of this sequence of numbers? Share your observations."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.311,
            0.746,
            0.332
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. What will be the digital root of the number "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "9a + 36b + 13?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.342,
            0.802,
            0.378
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4. Make conjectures by examining if there are any patterns or relations between"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.197,
            0.379,
            0.661,
            0.399
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) the parity of a number and its digital root."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.192,
            0.401,
            0.801,
            0.44
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) the digital root of a number and the remainder obtained when the number is divided by 3 or 9."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.807,
            0.307,
            0.906,
            0.436
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 9,
              "bbox": [
                0.807,
                0.307,
                0.906,
                0.436
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_19_image_9.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.469,
            0.439,
            0.494
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5.3 Digits in Disguise"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.503,
            0.849,
            0.559
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Last year, we saw cryptarithms—puzzles where each letter stands for a digit, each digit is represented by at most one letter, and the first digit of a number is never 0."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.569,
            0.503,
            0.592
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Solve the cryptarithms given below."
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.221,
            0.594,
            0.749,
            0.668
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "table_body",
              "index": 13,
              "bbox": [
                0.221,
                0.594,
                0.749,
                0.668
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_19_table_13.jpg",
              "content": "<table><tr><td><eq>\\frac { \\mathrm { ~ \\scriptsize ~ \\mathrm { ~ A 1 ~ } ~ } } { \\mathrm { ~ \\scriptsize ~ \\mathrm { ~ A B ~ } ~ } }</eq> (i) (ii)</td><td><eq>\\frac{\\frac{ AB }{1 + 37}}{6A}</eq> (iii)</td><td><eq>\\frac { \\begin{array} { c } { \\mathrm { O N } } \\\\ { \\mathrm { O N } } \\\\ { \\mathrm { O N } } \\end{array} } { \\begin{array} { c } { \\mathrm { P O } } \\end{array} }</eq> QR QR (iv) <eq>\\frac { \\mathrm { ~  ~ { ~ + ~ }  { Q \\mathrm { R } } ~ } } { \\mathrm { P R R } }</eq></td></tr></table>"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.671,
            0.802,
            0.692
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let us now try solving some cryptarithms involving multiplication."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.705,
            0.303,
            0.727
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(v) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "PQ \\times 8 = RS,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.731,
            0.667,
            0.859
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Guna says, “Oh, this means a 2-digit number multiplied by 8 should give another 2-digit number. I know that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "10 \\times 8 = 80"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . But the units digits of 10 and 80 are the same, which we don’t want. For the same reason PQ cannot be 11 as P and Q correspond to different digits. "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 2 \\times 8 = 9 6"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " fits all the conditions”. Can PQ be 13? Think."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.449,
            0.97,
            0.551,
            0.985
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.676,
            0.723,
            0.893,
            0.857
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 18,
              "bbox": [
                0.676,
